{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/tools/toolbox.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T21:10:53.953961Z","id":"dcc3396f54ad51aad6dc58a267c3993ca41361ebcdb91f404b0052dc5300ef9f","body":{"detail":"Toolbox.call refuses calls only when RunBudget.timeUp, and lets finish and give_up through even then. The turn, output-token and cost caps never refuse a call: they are reached when the turn that produced the calls is counted (RunBudget.addTurn), so refusing would throw away a turn already paid for, often the one that writes and renders the fix that stopAtCap could then publish. The runner checks RunBudget.hardStop before each model call instead. Covered by 'past the wall clock only finish and give_up still run' and 'the tools of the turn that reached the turn cap still run' in apps/clax_app/test/agent/tools/toolbox_test.dart.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":212},"end":{"line":235},"content_hash":"7825991fb2be3b12598985bfcac63fcdc84d19d9ce9e373042e280f5f7235492"},"summary":"Refuse every tool call once any hard cap is reached, not only once the wall clock is spent","tags":["agent","caps","revisit:a run is seen spending tool time (renders) after its turn, token or cost cap","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/tools/file_tools.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T21:10:53.954059Z","id":"3324cb4e943052e3dde50ee75a577ab3a10f61fff02f5264e13e77bb8879070d","body":{"detail":"A single line over maxReadBytes (64 KiB), such as a minified script, comes back cut at a code point boundary with truncated: true and a note; from_line cannot address inside a line, so the model can only str_replace a unique part it already knows or write_file the whole file. Pinned by 'cuts one line longer than 64 KiB and says so' in apps/clax_app/test/agent/tools/file_tools_test.dart.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":104},"end":{"line":118},"content_hash":"93ac1b4d79b41d7de362c8e7407c0a1abc287dda24c8aead54a6122d5294a9ad"},"suggested_fix":"If runs hit it, add a from_char offset to read_file, or split very long lines into 64 KiB windows.","summary":"read_file cannot read past 64 KiB of one line: a longer line is cut and its rest is unreachable","tags":["agent","tools","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/tools/draft.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T21:13:56.157292Z","id":"ac4e1490e8255375e101aa802f2016ea2d3900cf052ef31e936aa520bb33b3e2","body":{"detail":"Draft.markRendered({errors}) sets renderedRevision = _revision and lastClean = snapshot() at call time. A render (Task A5) snapshots the files, uploads them as the draft artifact, awaits Inspector.inspect for seconds, then marks. Toolbox.call (apps/clax_app/lib/agent/tools/toolbox.dart:212-235) does not serialize calls, and parallel tool_use blocks are commonly run concurrently (the Messages API guidance is to execute them concurrently). Inputs that break: one assistant turn with [render, write_file(index.html, broken)] run with Future.wait, or any runner that overlaps calls: write_file bumps the revision during the inspect await; markRendered(errors: false) then records the unrendered revision as renderedClean (the always-render-before-publish gate passes for files that never rendered) and stores them as lastClean (a cap stop publishes them). The test 'a clean render keeps a snapshot that later edits leave alone' (apps/clax_app/test/agent/tools/toolbox_test.dart:160) only covers a mark with no edit in between.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":174},"end":{"line":180},"content_hash":"64331fc421883b9e59a27a788905b70d8ef10d50825e7bc4eafcafe3e000c657"},"suggested_fix":"Make the render name what it rendered: DraftSnapshot s = draft.snapshot() before upload, then draft.markRendered(s, errors: e) sets renderedRevision = s.revision and, when clean, lastClean = s; renderedClean stays renderedRevision == revision. Also make Toolbox.call run one call at a time (a queue), as R§4.2 says ('in order, one at a time'). Test: an edit between snapshot and mark leaves renderedClean false and lastClean at the snapshot.","summary":"markRendered stamps the revision current when it is called, not the revision the render saw, so a draft edited during a render's await is marked rendered clean and kept as lastClean without ever having rendered","tags":["agent","draft","render","review:A1","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/tools/draft.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T21:13:56.157585Z","id":"82843b1cfc1adba2ca3d2527ba538fcd263f172dc535bcc368a3c8c98701c63e","body":{"detail":"Draft.reset moves baseVersion to the latest version and leaves 'render state for the caller to adjust'; lastClean (lines 102-103) still holds files built on the previous base, and DraftSnapshot (lines 12-43) has no baseVersion. R§4.5 resets the draft to the latest version when a touched path changed (Task A3's conflict reset); if the run then hits a hard cap before a new clean render, capStop publishes draft.lastClean with if_version = draft.baseVersion (the new latest), silently reverting the other change on every file the snapshot holds.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":140},"end":{"line":162},"content_hash":"4a3d435d1f535c8a8f8aa0e9842029e98b29e2863023bdfbdcb0a699835d8027"},"suggested_fix":"Give DraftSnapshot the baseVersion it was built on and have reset clear lastClean (or have capStop refuse a snapshot whose base is not draft.baseVersion); add a test in A3's capStop group.","summary":"A conflict reset keeps lastClean, which was rendered on the old base, and DraftSnapshot does not record its base version, so a cap stop after a reset can publish old-base files on top of the newer version","tags":["agent","draft","caps","review:A1","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/tools/budget.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T21:13:56.157778Z","id":"5670dbc29d9663b7df54d9c4c701c0e34de82a9f15b04d50dc59e92aa9f81538","body":{"detail":"RunBudget exposes timeUp and hardStop, which Toolbox.call (toolbox.dart:212-235) and the runner read before a call; nothing bounds work already started. A new-app turn streaming a full index.html at the end of the 90 s window, or a change turn started at 44 s, keeps going for as long as the model streams (tens of seconds on a large write), and finish/give_up stay exempt after it. R§1 RA3 asks for 'iterate, smooth, and quick' and R§4.4 sizes the caps so a change lands well under 30 s; the alternative dcc3396f (turn, token and cost caps never refuse) is sound for paid turns, but leaves time with no hard bound. The interface gives A4 no deadline to cancel a turn at: there is no remaining/deadline getter.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":160},"end":{"line":180},"content_hash":"058fd4d04209b1bab096b1f93392a97943a704bc9a4066c25f45d92ed196fb01"},"suggested_fix":"Add RunBudget.remaining (wall clock left, paused time excluded) and have MessagesApiRunner (A4) cancel the in-flight turn when it runs out, with a short grace, then stopAtCap with the last clean draft; pin it with an injected-clock test (hard_cap_mid_turn_cancels_the_turn).","summary":"The wall-clock cap is only checked between turns and tool calls: a model turn or render in flight when it passes runs to the end, so a 45 s change can run for 45 s plus a whole turn","tags":["agent","caps","review:A1","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/tools/draft.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T21:19:10.116612Z","id":"7e69f3f9ff3644bad73dd7393a08c6ba956db700c7995a84f1968cccf09606b4","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:01a47813","summary":"Fixed: Draft.markRendered(DraftSnapshot rendered, {errors}) records rendered.revision, so renderedClean holds only when nothing changed since the snapshot, and lastClean is the rendered snapshot; Toolbox.call runs calls one at a time in a queue. Tests in apps/clax_app/test/agent/tools/toolbox_test.dart: 'an edit between the snapshot and the mark is not rendered' and 'calls run one at a time, in order: a write during a render waits, and the draft is not marked clean' (a [render, write_file] pair made together). cd apps/clax_app && flutter test test/agent: +289, All tests passed.","supersedes":"ac4e1490e8255375e101aa802f2016ea2d3900cf052ef31e936aa520bb33b3e2","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/tools/draft.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T21:19:10.117234Z","id":"a834e55a32a4142d82d79bd1d9f02a5203f177c4b2a5e7d05ae8d94e9835c2aa","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:01a47813","summary":"Fixed: DraftSnapshot.baseVersion records the base it is built on; Draft.reset clears lastClean; markRendered never keeps a snapshot of another base; Draft.cleanOnBase is lastClean only when its base is the current one, and Toolbox.stopAtCap documents it as the only snapshot the cap handler (A3's capStop) may publish. Test 'a reset clears lastClean, and a snapshot of the old base is never kept' in apps/clax_app/test/agent/tools/toolbox_test.dart; A3's capStop group still has to pin the refusal. cd apps/clax_app && flutter test test/agent: +289, All tests passed.","supersedes":"82843b1cfc1adba2ca3d2527ba538fcd263f172dc535bcc368a3c8c98701c63e","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/tools/budget.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T21:19:10.118769Z","id":"1b8a416cbc2c9fe8b5b9481936483f123fb2c52e2ac5a866b4daeb8ecd87e3d6","body":{"detail":"Done in 01a47813 on the Toolbox side: RunBudget.remaining and RunBudget.whenTimeUp (paused while an ask waits; tests in apps/clax_app/test/agent/tools/budget_test.dart, group 'deadline'), and Toolbox.call refuses every call made once the wall clock is spent, finish and give_up included, while a call made before it runs (tests 'past the wall clock every call is refused, finish too' and 'a call made before the deadline runs, even if it starts after' in apps/clax_app/test/agent/tools/toolbox_test.dart). Open until MessagesApiRunner (Task A4) cancels the in-flight turn on whenTimeUp, pinned by hard_cap_mid_turn_cancels_the_turn.","kind":"comment","references":"5670dbc29d9663b7df54d9c4c701c0e34de82a9f15b04d50dc59e92aa9f81538","summary":"Decided under the owner's answer 'The experience should be iterate, smooth, and quick' (R§1 RA3 in docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-12-flutter-app-round2-design.md): the wall clock is a hard bound on work in flight. The runner cancels the turn in flight when RunBudget.whenTimeUp completes, then stops at the cap with the last clean draft; finish and give_up run only when called before the deadline.","tags":["status:decided","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/tools/toolbox.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T21:19:10.118865Z","id":"704b8ef426eb1e04a13c9693024fc8c77928e6de8926db0a3b9ab28d04c4f825","body":{"detail":"Toolbox.call refuses calls made once RunBudget.timeUp, finish and give_up included. The turn, output-token and cost caps never refuse a call: they are reached when the turn that produced the calls is counted (RunBudget.addTurn), so refusing would throw away a turn already paid for, often the one that writes and renders the fix that stopAtCap could then publish. The runner checks RunBudget.hardStop before each model call. Covered by 'past the wall clock every call is refused, finish too' and 'the tools of the turn that reached the turn cap still run' in apps/clax_app/test/agent/tools/toolbox_test.dart.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":212},"end":{"line":267},"content_hash":"9f5e1684c80ae646dac7d109eebebbd34aa5c67d2b04a3586678bd21841e0f6d"},"summary":"Refuse every tool call once any hard cap is reached, not only once the wall clock is spent","supersedes":"dcc3396f54ad51aad6dc58a267c3993ca41361ebcdb91f404b0052dc5300ef9f","tags":["agent","caps","revisit:a run is seen spending tool time (renders) after its turn, token or cost cap","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/tools/toolbox.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T21:20:12.225118Z","id":"6f65d22a710c76227771d2507dba0274601f3e40be0f49ca5e60b54c1a74c03b","body":{"detail":"Toolbox._queued chains every call and stopAtCap on _tail, and the cap handler (A3's FinishTool.capStop) runs inside the queued stopAtCap. If A3's finish/capStop, A5's render or A6's ask ever reaches the toolbox again (for example capStop calling toolbox.call('finish', …), or a tool calling stopAtCap on a cap it detects), that inner call queues behind the outer one and neither completes; nothing times out, so the run hangs. No current caller does this (lib/agent/tools/*.dart at 01a47813).","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":269},"end":{"line":273},"content_hash":"7ee032cec9f3f92e4cf41751ecffd280c611fe9dc9ab136513e2eb60dbeceea4"},"suggested_fix":"Say in the Tool and capHandler doc comments that they must act on RunState and the Draft directly, never through the Toolbox; or detect re-entry with a Zone value and fail fast with a StateError; a test in A3 that capStop completes.","summary":"Toolbox's call queue is not re-entrant: a tool or the cap handler that calls Toolbox.call or stopAtCap from inside a queued call waits on itself forever","tags":["agent","toolbox","review:A1","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/tools/render_tool.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T21:28:12.491338Z","id":"ed56b391096c79a2493c041c9111af3a4d68724451d0d30cff6e60ee61508203","body":{"detail":"RenderTool passes only ctx.cancelled to Inspector.inspect. RunBudget.whenTimeUp cancels the model turn in flight, not a tool call, so a page that never answers keeps render (and the Toolbox queue, toolbox.dart _queued) waiting for the WebViewInspector's own ready and inspection timeouts (R§5.2: 10 s each), up to 20 s of a change's 45 s. The runner that wires the run (A7) or the WebViewInspector (U6) should end the inspection when the wall clock runs out, for example by passing a future that completes on either the cancel or whenTimeUp.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":120},"end":{"line":136},"content_hash":"94575b100bd5fadddec6e188d2827bbd78491ad60a5ee0a5589f0e9a39a7c479"},"summary":"A render has no deadline of its own: a hung page holds the run for the Inspector's timeouts, unbounded by the run's wall clock","tags":["review","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/tools/render_tool.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T21:28:12.491552Z","id":"1d60b9e5add35188f94775975763a60aecf6e30fc525e3f3f8964e24fa71c639","body":{"detail":"R§5.2 asks for best effort, unpinned writes to the draft's copy. The daemon refuses an unpinned write to an existing document (if_version_required, docs/contract.md), so _writeDocs reads each document of the draft first (getDoc, in parallel) and pins the coalesced write to that version. A page that writes on load changes the copy between renders; the agent's staged op then lands over it in the copy, while finish pins the same op to the live version the agent read (draft.pins), so the copy and the live app can differ. The copy is a rendering aid; nothing from it reaches the app.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":261},"end":{"line":311},"content_hash":"e12c9b09bb1bc94ad898cee15c4b6ec132d01d511dbce780fd7acd632acb010b"},"summary":"Staged writes reach the draft's copy pinned to the copy's current version, so they overwrite what the page itself wrote there on an earlier render","tags":["review","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/tools/data_tools.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T21:28:38.870554Z","id":"c26896e49eebb29de0f82e75225eab722184e22e6bd11d968744bbe5e5b1e4e6","body":{"detail":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-12-flutter-app-round2-design.md R§3 (the paragraph after the tool table) says other apps' documents are read at the owner's level. _source here reads them with X-Clax-Reader set to RunContext.artifactId, so db_list, db_get and db_query of another app answer only while this app declares db.read of it and the owner granted it (or the source shares with it), and a new app (no artifactId) cannot read another app at all; the refusal points the model at the other apps' samples in the first message, which lib/agent/loop.dart _othersFrom still reads at the owner's level. Owner-level tool reads would let the agent build a cross-app feature (\"show my run totals on my dashboard\") before the consent exists; reader-only reads keep the agent inside the consent the page itself will need. Which one the tools follow is the owner's call.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":387},"end":{"line":400},"content_hash":"7b5ce0cd590aace47a473340c36c743e50f9660ec05329fcfc96dca843a1e137"},"summary":"Other apps' documents are read as this run's app (X-Clax-Reader), not at the owner's level as R§3 of the round-2 spec says","tags":["status:needs-decision","data-safety","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/tools/data_tools.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T21:28:38.871028Z","id":"2fcf878ecbdca7b16b51a2d47e55be676460b53f0c86bc2166473b7b81d41881","body":{"detail":"docs/superpowers/plans/2026-10-12-flutter-app-round2.md Task A2 and R§3 say at most 200 ops per run, but the daemon's docs:batch holds 1 to 50 writes (MAX_BATCH, crates/clax-core/src/store/docs.rs:51) and R§4.5 step 3 writes the staged ops in one batch so a refusal can restore the version before the change. 200 would need finish (lib/agent/tools/finish.dart, Task A3) to split the writes into batches that are not atomic together. revisit: if a change needs more than 50 document writes, add a daemon batch over 50 or a split write with its own undo.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":30},"end":{"line":32},"content_hash":"71079f5c0793c884d2b933712d2bff7d9f8808c3334cfc68486e64e9d44c57e8"},"summary":"A run stages at most 50 document writes (one docs:batch), not the 200 of the plan and R§3","tags":["revisit:more-than-50-writes","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/tools/data_tools.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T21:28:38.871212Z","id":"14b3ee96c99038d010cc8990e3d60737b68d89edebcfa81afeb380b6728fc9b6","body":{"detail":"GET docs:collections refuses X-Clax-Reader (record 79666ded, crates/clax-server/src/db_caller.rs), so DbCollectionsTool lists the collections at the owner's level and checks consent with listDocsAs on the first one. The counts include documents the source's view rules hide from a reader, and a source with no collections answers an empty list without any consent check (it shows only that there are none).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":100},"end":{"line":115},"content_hash":"7a0b13254a93802ed785efded9e42a0671da31503ae796a06b6069d95e568a16"},"summary":"db_collections of another app lists owner-level counts after a reader read of only its first collection","tags":["data-safety","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/tools/data_tools.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T21:28:38.871323Z","id":"dd5dfb4cab9cf7eda04cfb656f56f87b7c7893ad7a36b5c03c21864229f4d9f5","body":{"detail":"DbWriteTool refuses a second write to a document already staged this run (the daemon refuses a docs:batch naming a document twice), and _pin (line 472) never moves the pin of a staged document when it is read again, so finish can batch Draft.stagedDb as is with if_version from Draft.pins (null: the document did not exist when staged). A document the first message showed is pinned to RunContext.shownDocs's version on its first staged write.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":325},"end":{"line":370},"content_hash":"ba964246329eb3d938506d8d2fab6edb2e156f61fd01451c26e6bd937cff62be"},"summary":"For finish (Task A3): every staged document appears once, and its Draft.pins entry is the version the write was staged on","tags":["handoff","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/tools/budget.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T21:31:47.188389Z","id":"8ba8cca35ea905d032b966fbae571439cbfe5a1be90115f7b975a0ece4492861","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:a0f7f151","summary":"Fixed in a0f7f151: MessagesApiRunner (apps/clax_app/lib/agent/runner/messages_runner.dart) passes a stop signal as the turn's cancel and fires it when RunBudget.whenTimeUp completes; the backend aborts the request and closes its connection, and the run stops at the wall-clock cap through Toolbox.stopAtCap with the latest narration. Test 'caps hard_cap_mid_turn_cancels_the_turn' in apps/clax_app/test/agent/runner/messages_runner_test.dart (a turn left streaming on a raw-socket server, the injected clock advanced 45 s: outcome RunGaveUp('45 seconds') from the cap handler, the server sees the connection close, the draft unchanged) fails with the whenTimeUp listener commented out and passes with it. flutter test test/agent: +387, All tests passed.","supersedes":"5670dbc29d9663b7df54d9c4c701c0e34de82a9f15b04d50dc59e92aa9f81538","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/tools/budget.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T21:31:47.189118Z","id":"41433e5e581b66179ef07a2c784a4c8303b6b8d045c5ba93d61a990de0f8c8d9","body":{"detail":"After a run ends early, RunBudget._waitTimeUp no longer waits on it (it races the delay against the end and then never completes), so nothing acts on the deadline; only the timer itself stays scheduled until the original deadline (at most 90 s on the wall clock) and then wakes nothing. Cancelling it needs a cancellable delay on Clock (apps/clax_app/lib/daemon/clock.dart), which five test clocks also implement.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":185},"end":{"line":200},"content_hash":"f4a6b4b09b8c6eb72e82dcb9accd20198176716976541b11f9539cb106f412d7"},"summary":"endClock stops whenTimeUp from completing, but the Clock's own pending delay still runs to the deadline: SystemClock.delay is a Future.delayed timer that Clock cannot cancel","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/tools/render_tool.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T21:33:36.234221Z","id":"1e37add8fac0a3afcc1e38e256a20fbe5626cb2017a99c16f9881b24de466de6","body":{"detail":"Failure: a change run whose agent edits only app.js or style.css (or deletes a file, or changes only the title or capabilities) and renders: _publish sends files = only the changed paths, the daemon answers 400 missing_index ('index.html is required on every publish', crates/clax-core/src/publish.rs:261-269; docs/contract.md publish: index.html is the page and must be in every publish, other files carry forward), and render answers 'The draft could not be served: index.html is required on every publish.' after spending one of the run's 2 renders. Every later render fails the same way until index.html changes, so finish's render-before-publish gate never passes and the run ends without the change. Reproduced against a real daemon (target/debug/clax at f64a72a8, scratch CLAX_HOME): render 1 created the draft, render 2 (index.html and app.js changed) published v2, render 3 after deleteFile('app.js') was refused with that message, as was every render after it. The unit tests pass because FakeClaxApi.publishDraft checks the merged file set, not the request (apps/clax_app/lib/clax/fake_api.dart:784-795).","kind":"blocker","span":{"start":{"line":224},"end":{"line":256},"content_hash":"45aa200b596aff549d5537d14056508146977cd9d042661a1893b318105f234d"},"suggested_fix":"Always put snap.files['index.html'] in the publish's files (the render already refuses a draft without it); keep sending only the other files that changed. Test: an edit to app.js alone renders and publishes, against a fake that refuses a request without index.html as the daemon does.","summary":"An incremental draft publish leaves out an unchanged index.html, and the daemon refuses every publish without it, so any render after the first that did not change index.html fails","tags":["review","review:A5","draft","render","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/tools/render_tool.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T21:33:36.234343Z","id":"514df435a51a325cbc4eb84c65e4cdf031fd92242262dfbd57dcb9a8c29456ea","body":{"detail":"docs/contract.md db_update: nested objects merge field by field, {\"__delete__\": true} removes its field, other values replace. _coalesce does {...prev.data, ...o.data}. Inputs that break: set runs/r9 {a:{x:1,y:1}, gone:1} then update {a:{y:2}, gone:{__delete__:true}} in one render. Against a real daemon the draft write was refused ('{\"__delete__\": true} removes a field only in an update', listed in db_refused) while the same two ops written one by one to the app give {a:{x:1,y:2}}. update+update on a nested object likewise drops the earlier nested fields ({a:{x:1}} then {a:{y:2}} renders as {a:{y:2}}). The render then shows data finish will not write, and the agent may 'fix' a page that was right.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":401},"end":{"line":420},"content_hash":"199fd0d03054d3730701ebcd1173151f64fce244a666da05806d3a513197336b"},"suggested_fix":"Merge as the daemon does: for an update onto a set, deep-merge objects and drop fields marked __delete__; for update onto update, deep-merge and keep __delete__ markers. Or skip coalescing and write each staged op in order, pinning each to the version the previous one produced. Test both shapes against the contract's merge rule.","summary":"_coalesce folds staged writes with a shallow merge, but the daemon's update merges nested objects and treats {\"__delete__\": true} as a removal, so the draft copy the page renders over differs from what the same ops make, and a set+update with __delete__ is refused","tags":["review","review:A5","draft","db","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/tools/render_tool.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T21:33:36.234431Z","id":"f55cb16a4b21806fdcbbe15dc75970ea5dca2432ef8133bb70aa27103fb107ad","body":{"detail":"Toolbox.stopAtCap queues behind the call in flight (apps/clax_app/lib/agent/tools/toolbox.dart _queued), so a hung page holds even the wall-clock cap stop until the Inspector's own 10 s + 10 s timeouts (R§5.2) end the inspect: a change capped at 45 s can run to about 65 s, and a slow-but-alive page eats most of a quick change's budget. RenderTool has everything it needs (s.budget.whenTimeUp, s.budget.remaining, s.ctx.clock) to bound the inspect itself.","kind":"concern","references":"ed56b391096c79a2493c041c9111af3a4d68724451d0d30cff6e60ee61508203","span":{"start":{"line":121},"end":{"line":126},"content_hash":"4982df668a7d31a43efdb9e997f7ac61ec5666a2ff5714557f24dc617c6914da"},"suggested_fix":"Pass inspector.inspect a cancelled future that completes on the first of ctx.cancelled, s.budget.whenTimeUp and s.ctx.clock.delay(min(s.budget.remaining, 8 s)); when the deadline (not the cancel) ends it, mark the snapshot rendered with errors and answer 'The page did not load within 8 s …' so the agent can act. Test with StepClock: a hung page returns an error result once the clock passes 8 s, and once the run's remaining time is spent, whichever is first.","summary":"Decision for A5 (reviewer): the render takes its own deadline now; ed56b391 is not left to A7/U6","tags":["review","review:A5","render","caps","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/tools/data_tools.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T22:49:45.933265Z","id":"3d0bb96d9453af625d544a8e1f5b2b427f194eb7cd7f7c73e8b994536d5c91ae","body":{"detail":"Verbatim, as relayed: \"User must give consent for this action separately from an app reading data. They may not want 'corruption' across app boundaries.\" Implemented in f916b348: apps/clax_app/lib/agent/read_consent.dart AgentReadConsent (once | always | denied, always remembered per (this app, source app) pair behind the interface), held by RunState.readConsent; _source in apps/clax_app/lib/agent/tools/data_tools.dart asks it before any db_* read of another app, at most once a run with the wall clock paused, then reads at the owner's level without X-Clax-Reader and without needing the app's db.read declaration; denied answers \"The owner did not allow reading <title>.\" Recorded by an agent from a relayed answer, so the owner confirms it under their own identity.","kind":"comment","references":"c26896e49eebb29de0f82e75225eab722184e22e6bd11d968744bbe5e5b1e4e6","summary":"Owner's answer, relayed by the coordinator of the round-2 build on 2026-10-12: the agent reads another app's documents only with the owner's own consent, separate from an app's runtime db.read","tags":["status:needs-decision:mailto:kesling@empathic.dev","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/tools/data_tools.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T22:49:45.933811Z","id":"4537c36af1e597be1ebae01f7562ac25a14083e0e5f57cc9e45a3ed29cb0022a","body":{"detail":"docs/superpowers/plans/2026-10-12-flutter-app-round2.md Task A2 and R§3 say at most 200 ops per run, but the daemon's docs:batch holds 1 to 50 writes (MAX_BATCH, crates/clax-core/src/store/docs.rs:51) and R§4.5 step 3 writes the staged ops in one batch so a refusal can restore the version before the change. 200 would need finish (lib/agent/tools/finish.dart, Task A3) to split the writes into batches that are not atomic together. revisit: if a change needs more than 50 document writes, add a daemon batch over 50 or a split write with its own undo.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":32},"end":{"line":34},"content_hash":"71079f5c0793c884d2b933712d2bff7d9f8808c3334cfc68486e64e9d44c57e8"},"summary":"A run stages at most 50 document writes (one docs:batch), not the 200 of the plan and R§3","supersedes":"2fcf878ecbdca7b16b51a2d47e55be676460b53f0c86bc2166473b7b81d41881","tags":["revisit:more-than-50-writes","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/tools/data_tools.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T22:49:45.935649Z","id":"bde7e5cb3e262d3d272cd369886b9d05d38640c18174dd8aa170272190e6844c","body":{"detail":"DbWriteTool refuses a second write to a document already staged this run (the daemon refuses a docs:batch naming a document twice), and _pin (apps/clax_app/lib/agent/tools/data_tools.dart, the function after _stagedOp) never moves the pin of a staged document when it is read again, so finish can batch Draft.stagedDb as is with if_version from Draft.pins (null: the document did not exist when staged). A document the first message showed is pinned to RunContext.shownDocs's version on its first staged write.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":308},"end":{"line":353},"content_hash":"04d279df6acff5417bbbfc3982f1d48be5fa8b51ae9a85010835629a481b8717"},"summary":"For finish (Task A3): every staged document appears once, and its Draft.pins entry is the version the write was staged on","supersedes":"dd5dfb4cab9cf7eda04cfb656f56f87b7c7893ad7a36b5c03c21864229f4d9f5","tags":["handoff","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/tools/data_tools.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T22:49:59.375796Z","id":"efb4362b9477b3f9f6c14f1fd29dc15c6db7b354b91b750eb3212923f161cc30","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f916b348","summary":"f916b348 removed the reader read: db_collections of another app now runs only after AgentReadConsent and lists at the owner's level, without data/users/ collections. flutter test test/agent/tools/data_tools_test.dart: 44 passed (\"another app's collections need the owner's consent\").","supersedes":"14b3ee96c99038d010cc8990e3d60737b68d89edebcfa81afeb380b6728fc9b6","tags":["reason:obsolete","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/tools/render_tool.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T22:55:47.155122Z","id":"992b2c841161ffc2560dd66a333b0736e767d860ab0131782e0a1af948bbf3cf","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:b290498a","summary":"Every draft publish now names index.html with the changed files (render_tool.dart _publish). Evidence: test/agent/tools/render_tool_real_test.dart against a real debug clax (CLAX_TEST_BIN=target/clax-bin/debug/42e64e10…/clax) renders after a delete-only, a title-only and an app.js-only change and passes ('+1: All tests passed!'); with d2d57d3f's render_tool.dart it fails with 'ToolRefused(The draft could not be served: index.html is required on every publish.)'. Unit tests 'a removed file…', 'a change to app.js alone…' and 'a title-only change…' in render_tool_test.dart pass (27/27).","supersedes":"1e37add8fac0a3afcc1e38e256a20fbe5626cb2017a99c16f9881b24de466de6","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/tools/render_tool.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T22:55:47.155859Z","id":"e8cf2fbb23399ec9be3dd5516ecc04252d038e8ae0e6a8d4861c1472af82ed2c","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:b290498a","summary":"Staged writes are no longer coalesced: _writeDocs sends them in order, in rounds of writes to distinct documents, each pinned to the copy's version just before it, so the daemon applies its own merge. Evidence: render_tool_real_test.dart stages set runs/r9 {a:{x:1,y:1},gone:1} then update {a:{y:2},gone:{__delete__:true}} and reads {a:{x:1,y:2}} from the real daemon's draft with no db_refused (passes); render_tool_test.dart 'staged writes reach the draft one by one in order…' passes.","supersedes":"514df435a51a325cbc4eb84c65e4cdf031fd92242262dfbd57dcb9a8c29456ea","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/tools/render_tool.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T22:55:47.156483Z","id":"eb16dbbf7fea69859634521938e46107aeb50482992426d4b49f96ac627633c9","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:b290498a","summary":"The render now bounds its inspection by the first of the run's cancel, budget.whenTimeUp and clock.delay(min(remaining, inspectLimit = 8 s)), racing the inspector so one that ignores its signal cannot hold the run; a timed-out render is marked rendered with errors (the decision in reply f55cb16a). Evidence: render_tool_test.dart group 'deadline' (StepClock: not done at 7.999 s, refused naming 8 seconds at 8 s; out of time at the 45 s wall clock after 40 + 5 s; a stuck inspector released at 8 s) passes, 27/27.","supersedes":"ed56b391096c79a2493c041c9111af3a4d68724451d0d30cff6e60ee61508203","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/tools/data_tools.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T22:55:49.912938Z","id":"a047a318105e2b30b987a4039be543c008b0e90ac4e7a566bbdfc3424f8dd27f","body":{"detail":"_source awaits AgentReadConsent.ask (apps/clax_app/lib/agent/read_consent.dart:21-34, no cancellation argument) between pauseClock and resumeClock. MessagesApiRunner awaits each toolbox.call before it checks _cancelled (apps/clax_app/lib/agent/runner/messages_runner.dart:190-197), and RunBudget.timeUp never fires while the clock is paused (apps/clax_app/lib/agent/tools/budget.dart:140-160). Inputs that break: a change run by the feedback worker asks to read app B while the owner is away, or the owner cancels the change while the dialog is up: the run holds its worker slot, its draft and its consent dialog until someone answers. render_tool.dart watches RunContext.cancelled (CancelWatch, line 92); this wait does not.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":389},"end":{"line":404},"content_hash":"542eab4838a4824cd369ce3c4cd05a62d45e9ad755b0edfeb9b068564d71264b"},"suggested_fix":"Race consent.ask against s.ctx.cancelled and answer the call as cancelled (ToolRefused, clock resumed) when the run is cancelled; pass a cancelled future through AgentReadConsent.ask so U6's dialog closes with it. Test: a FakeReadConsent whose answer never completes, cancel the run, the db_list call returns and the clock runs again.","summary":"The owner's read-consent question cannot be cancelled, and the wall clock is paused while it waits, so a cancelled or unattended run waits on it forever","tags":["review","review:A2","consent","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/tools/data_tools.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T22:55:49.913028Z","id":"b1076e994606f9d7fe1a04a8d6f647b8f2639aa82ae0229c94536bb2e48fa07a","body":{"detail":"_op checks only that data_json is a JSON object of at most 256 KiB as sent. Store check_body (crates/clax-core/src/store/docs.rs:338-390) also refuses: {\"__delete__\": true} in a set, inside an array, or as the whole body; a body over MAX_DEPTH (32) levels; and the size is of the stored JSON, so an update that merges a read document past 256 KiB is refused too. Inputs that break: db_write [{op: set, collection: settings, doc_id: main, data_json: '{\"old\": {\"__delete__\": true}}'}] stages as {staged: 1}; finish sends it in the one docs:batch with the change's other writes and the daemon refuses the whole batch. The model learns this only after the run has ended, when it can no longer fix the op.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":476},"end":{"line":519},"content_hash":"3164251280bdcc98541c5a74f0610c7fb0aedfb942ace21fc080c3259a3e8db1"},"suggested_fix":"Mirror check_body in _op: refuse __delete__ markers outside update or inside arrays, the whole-body marker, and depth over 32; for an update of a document this run read, measure the merged body (deep merge as docs/contract.md db_update describes) against 256 KiB. One test per shape.","summary":"db_write stages bodies the daemon refuses, so one bad op fails finish's all-or-nothing batch and every document write of the change is lost","tags":["review","review:A2","db","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/tools/data_tools.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T22:55:49.913092Z","id":"8e28d31457a1943c2e7b9305c91a326b40147d8907e9b73acc671ca97c121405","body":{"detail":"Rules::self_prefixes (crates/clax-core/src/db.rs:274-292) makes data/users and the prefix of every declared {self} rule private per viewer, and Rules::allows (db.rs:394-407) refuses them to a caller whose viewer is not that viewer; the app's token caller has no viewer (base_caller, crates/clax-server/src/db_caller.rs:195-215). Reads stay safe: doc_get answers None (docs.rs:721-731) and doc_collections leaves those collections out (docs.rs:700-719). But with a rule {path: 'prefs/{self}'}: db_get prefs/u_x/items/a answers exists: false and pins it absent, the existence probe in db_write (data_tools.dart:333) also sees nothing, and a set stages; finish's docs:batch is then refused whole, as in the record on _op. The model is also told a private document does not exist, rather than that it is private.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":599},"end":{"line":599},"content_hash":"769018f9ac93bc00763ab7c6e15c93934ffb7959a62e28546d66350795cb42ca"},"suggested_fix":"Derive the private prefixes from the app's capabilities (RunContext.capabilities and Draft's set_meta value: db.rules entries ending in {self}) as well as data/users, and refuse reads and writes under them with _privateError.","summary":"Only data/users/ is treated as private; a subtree an app declares private with a {self} rule reads as absent and its writes stage, then fail the finish batch","tags":["review","review:A2","db","privacy","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/tools/toolbox.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T22:55:49.913220Z","id":"2a1b743e32b3b376e3cfc1ccd3760b5da95b1ab72a8b19f76e8e915b8d5e2745","body":{"detail":"DbWriteTool takes a pin from shownDocs keyed by bare document path (apps/clax_app/lib/agent/tools/data_tools.dart:329-330). The first message still carries other apps' sample documents (record 990b6fef on apps/clax_app/lib/agent/loop.dart). If the caller that builds RunContext fills shownDocs from every sample, a write to this app's notes/n1 is pinned to the version of another app's notes/n1: refused at finish when the versions differ, and a write over a document the agent never saw when they match.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":99},"end":{"line":101},"content_hash":"0115e5f4462951d14e257a984fc22fb308115e23971a195a739e05fe3473953d"},"suggested_fix":"Doc comment: 'This app's documents only.' and a test in the caller that builds RunContext that other apps' samples are left out.","summary":"Say that RunContext.shownDocs holds this app's documents only: db_write pins its writes to these versions","tags":["review","review:A2","db","task:A7","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/tools/render_tool.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T22:57:55.070722Z","id":"9bc36f420f33e33445c747a4a233e393a1a2f4291ff8c5ab26dbf4e0116e7c2f","body":{"detail":"R§5.2 asks for best effort, unpinned writes to the draft's copy. The daemon refuses an unpinned write to an existing document (if_version_required, docs/contract.md), so _writeDocs sends the staged writes in order, in rounds of writes to distinct documents, each pinned to the version the copy holds just before its round (_writeRound reads it with getDoc). A page that writes on load changes the copy between renders; the agent's staged op then lands over it in the copy, while finish pins the same op to the live version the agent read (draft.pins), so the copy and the live app can differ. The copy is a rendering aid; nothing from it reaches the app. Checked against a real daemon: a page update to runs/r1 in the copy followed by staged update, update, delete, set leaves the copy at the set's data and the app's document unchanged.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":298},"end":{"line":378},"content_hash":"579d92f68fff170e15d43223e9b86d895d99b6b5849d3b19b967fbe0067d4933"},"summary":"Staged writes reach the draft's copy pinned to the copy's current version, so they overwrite what the page itself wrote there on an earlier render","supersedes":"1d60b9e5add35188f94775975763a60aecf6e30fc525e3f3f8964e24fa71c639","tags":["review","draft","db","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/tools/render_tool.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T22:57:55.072626Z","id":"15e5c3c7e8fb80195472e9aac6b36449a2f632ba3d789bc4d2cd6836dab00665","body":{"kind":"resolve","summary":"Done in b290498a: render races the inspection against the first of the run's cancel, budget.whenTimeUp and clock.delay(min(remaining, 8 s)) (render_tool.dart inspectLimit). flutter test test/agent/tools/render_tool_test.dart: +27 All tests passed, including the deadline group ('a page that does not answer in 8 seconds is a failed render', 'near the end of the wall clock the render waits only for what is left', 'an inspector that ignores the deadline does not hold the render').","supersedes":"f55cb16a4b21806fdcbbe15dc75970ea5dca2432ef8133bb70aa27103fb107ad","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/tools/data_tools.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T23:00:35.153306Z","id":"a1aef48acf4978585091229be9f07111e23eedb820c8131d67cca8f2cdf5d0db","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:be4c9aa0","summary":"Fixed in be4c9aa0: AgentReadConsent.ask takes the run's cancelled future (apps/clax_app/lib/agent/read_consent.dart), and _askOwner in data_tools.dart races the question against RunContext.cancelled, answering denied for the run and resuming the wall clock; a run already cancelled before the question does not ask. cd apps/clax_app && flutter test test/agent/tools/data_tools_test.dart: 56 passed, including 'a cancelled run answers the question as denied' and 'a run cancelled before it asks does not ask'.","supersedes":"a047a318105e2b30b987a4039be543c008b0e90ac4e7a566bbdfc3424f8dd27f","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/tools/data_tools.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T23:00:35.204634Z","id":"af5efc5754be8f06518c1a938b6d144b78f4cc20d1fc3190103e85373cf2e3ff","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:be4c9aa0","summary":"Fixed in be4c9aa0: _bodyProblem in data_tools.dart applies check_body (crates/clax-core/src/store/docs.rs:343) to every set and update body (delete markers only as an update's field value, never in an array or as the whole body; at most 32 levels; 256 KiB as JSON), and an update's body merged into the current document (_merged, a port of merge_into) is checked again before it stages. cd apps/clax_app && flutter test test/agent/tools/data_tools_test.dart: 56 passed, group 'db_write bodies' (5 tests).","supersedes":"b1076e994606f9d7fe1a04a8d6f647b8f2639aa82ae0229c94536bb2e48fa07a","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/tools/data_tools.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T23:00:35.255989Z","id":"48f8976acbdbd7b271e8b53132f69bc70c5b2191c9cb10627f5beb64f5ea2986","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:be4c9aa0","summary":"Fixed in be4c9aa0: _privatePrefixes in data_tools.dart follows Rules::self_prefixes and private_to (crates/clax-core/src/db.rs): data/users plus each {self} rule's prefix that no rule at the prefix opens, from the live and the draft's declarations for this app and from the source's for another app. db_get, db_list, db_query and db_write refuse such paths as private, and db_collections leaves those collections out. cd apps/clax_app && flutter test test/agent/tools/data_tools_test.dart: 56 passed, group 'private subtrees' (5 tests).","supersedes":"8e28d31457a1943c2e7b9305c91a326b40147d8907e9b73acc671ca97c121405","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/tools/toolbox.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T23:00:35.306579Z","id":"7031162db7162670a3574c866710679b7ce9a3e466d92fa96684884388a33c41","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:be4c9aa0","summary":"Fixed in be4c9aa0: RunContext.shownDocs's doc comment (apps/clax_app/lib/agent/tools/toolbox.dart) says it holds this app's documents only, never another app's samples, since db_write pins by path alone. Filling it is A7's (record 990b6fef on loop.dart).","supersedes":"2a1b743e32b3b376e3cfc1ccd3760b5da95b1ab72a8b19f76e8e915b8d5e2745","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/tools/finish.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T23:13:37.491584Z","id":"8ac3085d17c79d4cac81103c2fd83ab13091c1ea3b251bcf1cf81db86f85f02b","body":{"detail":"Not taken: a re-pinned set or delete replaces or removes what the person wrote since the run read the document, and a re-pinned update overwrites every field its patch names, including an entry the person added to an array field (docs/superpowers/plans/2026-10-12-flutter-app-round2.md Review Focus 1: never overwrite the person's entry). The finish tool's _writeDocs re-reads instead and only drops a write the moved document already holds (a delete of a gone document, a set or update that changes nothing); a moved document that does not hold the write fails the change, after restoring the version before it, and the threads offer Retry. Cost: a change whose update touches fields the person did not change (round 1's 'a document conflict re-reads and writes once more', apps/clax_app/test/agent/loop_test.dart:614) now fails instead of merging. The draft keeps only the version each document was read at (Draft.pins), not its data, so a field-level check of what the person changed is not possible here.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":823},"end":{"line":866},"content_hash":"5adec366627eb4e2424742be9d0787a22046abc9ccfc1e07e4c8edbf999dd3cf"},"summary":"On a document conflict at finish, re-pin each write to the version read again and send it once more (the round-1 _writeDocs rule, lib/agent/loop.dart:778-812, and R§4.5 step 3's 'one re-read and retry')","tags":["agent","finish","data-safety","revisit:changes fail often because the page wrote a document mid-run","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/tools/finish.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T23:13:37.491703Z","id":"e260cdd0b2dd761f8aeed2466fc6564cb7ef4d3a72bbb30cc711c4a964f6bdf9","body":{"detail":"The gate counts a staged db_write as a change (Draft.changedFrom), so a documents-only change must render clean before finish writes the owner's data, as a file change must. Not taken because a render over the draft's document copy is the only check that the page still loads with the new data; it costs one render turn (a change has 2) on a data-only answer.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":200},"end":{"line":224},"content_hash":"4b76645a45ae7b738c25126d9361f5268b39f9e57373b82dc3c6f972e83de41d"},"summary":"Let a finish whose only change is staged document writes skip the render","tags":["agent","finish","revisit:data-only changes need their render budget for something else","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/tools/finish.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T23:13:37.491755Z","id":"00f142bc0a6d8ea7ac47382642084468b3c1be39743828ee445dd1fc89f353cc","body":{"detail":"capStop publishes the last clean snapshot of a new app; finish refuses a new app without a title, but a cap cannot ask the model again, so _create falls back to the title the render served the draft under (RenderTool's _untitled, apps/clax_app/lib/agent/tools/render_tool.dart). The owner sees an app named 'New app' and renames it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":315},"end":{"line":325},"content_hash":"6b6933d6a52963ec1d3d11ed0c4fda6f23176885a9be87669dce9123eee9a514"},"suggested_fix":"Have A7 pass a title derived from the request (its first words) for a cap stop, or have the prompt (assets/prompt/system.md) ask for set_meta before the first render.","summary":"A new app stopped at a cap before set_meta gave it a title is created as 'New app'","tags":["agent","caps","new-app","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/tools/finish.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T23:13:37.491814Z","id":"684d15e9c2f996691cc7fa3923d284974e90b6d16a7e858be65eb3567d2e2492","body":{"detail":"Without attach, Toolbox.stopAtCap gives up naming the cap and nothing is replied. Outcomes: RunFinished (version null when only replied or only documents were written; a cap that published a clean snapshot is also RunFinished, with the stopped-early reply and no resolve), RunGaveUp (give_up, a cap with no clean draft, refused data, a second publish conflict; answered says the threads got the reply), RunCancelled, RunInterrupted (ledger record kept), RunDropped. newerComments, madeBy and cleanLine are the top-level copies settle can use once loop.dart's originals go. Runner-made endings (records 86ca4f33, 691f40a8) still need A7 to reply and clean up.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":147},"end":{"line":152},"content_hash":"260abc1776075b15a7f3d53e62a9ef7ea1e112bdd9f32fa18bbed1546bb31807"},"summary":"For A7 (AgentLoop on runners): call FinishTool.attach(toolbox) so capStop is the cap handler; finish, give_up and capStop clear the working mark and call RenderTool.cleanup themselves","tags":["handoff","agent","finish","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/tools/data_tools.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T23:13:37.491884Z","id":"d6975284d533c23af0b5e868032639e5d445495c90c8a12291f83785691ce90a","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"bde7e5cb3e262d3d272cd369886b9d05d38640c18174dd8aa170272190e6844c","summary":"Consumed by apps/clax_app/lib/agent/tools/finish.dart's _writeDocs (d8baf675): Draft.stagedDb goes as one docs:batch with if_version from Draft.pins; test 'staged writes go in one batch pinned to the versions read, after the publish' in apps/clax_app/test/agent/tools/finish_test.dart.","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/tools/toolbox.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T23:13:37.491934Z","id":"3a206c4cec3a6d5bfa77dc6d6795b3718b339f64ec23eab1ed785cd49a223e85","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"6f65d22a710c76227771d2507dba0274601f3e40be0f49ca5e60b54c1a74c03b","summary":"FinishTool.capStop (apps/clax_app/lib/agent/tools/finish.dart, d8baf675) acts on RunState and the Draft only and never calls the Toolbox; test 'capStop runs inside the Toolbox queue and completes' in apps/clax_app/test/agent/tools/finish_test.dart stops at a cap while a render is queued and gets RunFinished. The doc-comment or re-entry guard the suggestion names is still open.","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/tools/finish.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T23:22:28.022792Z","id":"49ce8342aa876818c3e78ed2a455075afd6da3cd1f2899f992c6833b8db5fe96","body":{"detail":"_writeDocs (finish.dart:823-866) re-reads every staged document after a batch conflict with api.getDoc; a getDoc that throws a ClaxApiError with a status other than 0 (a 500, a 503) escapes _writeDocs, skips the restore at finish.dart:481-490 and lands in _change's outer catch (finish.dart:517-528 or 529-532), which replies \"Couldn't make that change: <message>\" and ends RunGaveUp. Reproduced with the finish_test.dart Rig: stage set runs/b, edit, render, then on the live batch failNext('batchDocs', 409 conflict) and failNext('getDoc', 500 internal) -> outcome RunGaveUp, current version 2 (the published page), restoreVersion called 0 times, ledger still holds base 1 with docsDone false, reply \"Couldn't make that change: db busy\". So the person sees the new version without the documents it was rendered with, and the kept record lets a later settle (loop.dart settle, record d359fbc3's rule) send the batch at the old pins and write the documents after the thread was told the change failed. Related, same block: a restore refused with a non-zero status (finish.dart:485-488, for example 409 because someone published after the landed version) is logged and the record forgotten, so the landed version without its data also stays; and a batch answered 404 not_found (the app deleted after the publish) ends RunGaveUp, not RunDropped. No test covers a re-read failure, a refused restore, or a 404 batch.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":479},"end":{"line":532},"content_hash":"2890bad3b8c67080dcfeee44fb4fd748241bf67f8d7d5fb44e84680534bc3fac"},"suggested_fix":"After a landed publish, treat every failure of the document step except status 0 as a refusal: catch inside _writeDocs's re-read (return the message) or wrap the call at finish.dart:480 so any non-status-0 error goes through the restore and _forget; add the Rig test above asserting restoreVersion(n: 1, ifVersion: 2), current version 3 with the base files, and an empty ledger.","summary":"A failure other than a refusal while writing the documents after the publish landed (a re-read getDoc that errors, any non-ClaxApiError) skips the restore and keeps the ledger record: the new page stays live without its data","tags":["agent","finish","data-safety","review:A3","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/tools/finish.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T23:22:28.022942Z","id":"2193e695ee47072ca8b4451171f50ae51f8b8e1afdb3825f7371bbe5137ec561","body":{"detail":"_create logs a refused or failed batch (finish.dart:344-353) and returns RunFinished(version: 1) with the note claiming the app was made. The draft's render (RenderTool) served the page over the draft's document copy holding the staged writes, so the page that rendered clean is not the page the person gets. This is the round-1 rule carried over from loop.dart newApp (open record 8824e56f on apps/clax_app/lib/agent/loop.dart says the same and why throwing would let the New sheet's Retry duplicate the app); with A7 deleting loop.dart's original, the open edge now lives here. Not covered by finish_test.dart (no test refuses a new app's batch). A createArtifact without an answer (status 0, finish.dart:338-340) ends RunInterrupted with no ledger record for new apps, so whether an app was made is unknown to recovery.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":344},"end":{"line":358},"content_hash":"8211ec7bea469564fdee99ffd93d86aeb140387598957a99e8bcc76d678b5e48"},"suggested_fix":"Carry the refusal in the outcome (for example RunFinished with a warning, or append a sentence to the version note through a follow-up publish) so A7's making screen can say the starting data was not saved; decide with A7 how a status-0 createArtifact is recovered without a duplicate.","summary":"A new app whose starting documents are refused after createArtifact is reported as RunFinished with nothing to tell the person; the app the render checked had that data, the live one does not","tags":["agent","finish","new-app","review:A3","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/tools/finish.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T23:22:28.023092Z","id":"2093755bacda5c898b1efdaeb633ca71cf0cfb7773a164769107899c001b6e5b","body":{"detail":"Verified against a real debug clax (apps/clax_app/test/support/real_daemon.dart with CLAX_TEST_BIN): an update staged on log/today read at its first version, the document then set to runs ['5 km','3 km'] before finish; finish ended RunGaveUp \"its data couldn't be updated: log/today was changed while I worked, and I did not write over it\", the document kept ['5 km','3 km'], versions 1, 2, 3 with v3's files equal to v1's, the ledger empty and no draft left. Fake coverage: finish_test.dart 'finish_never_overwrites_a_document_the_person_changed_mid_run', 'a person who creates the document a set would create is never written over', 'a document created meanwhile with the same data is not written again'.","kind":"comment","references":"8ac3085d17c79d4cac81103c2fd83ab13091c1ea3b251bcf1cf81db86f85f02b","summary":"Decided (by the coordinating agent of the round-2 build, issuer_type ai, not the owner): keep the implemented rule. A document that moved since the run read it and does not already hold the write is never written over; the version before the change is restored with if_version set to the landed version, and the threads get \"Couldn't make that change: its data couldn't be updated: ...\" and offer Retry. Reason: data safety. A re-pinned write would replace an entry the person added on the page mid-run (an array field replaced whole by an update), and losing the person's data is worse than a failed change that Retry re-runs on the current document.","tags":["status:decided","agent","finish","data-safety","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/tools/ask_tool.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T23:23:46.066708Z","id":"852bbee73692d54e1b3886dc8283eb27cf7e5e891fc573606dac58f5dccf4976","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-mcp/src/tools.rs do_ask waits timeout_s whatever surface_open says. The app's AskTool answers at once with status open, call_again true and surface_open false instead: with no stream holding questions or inbox for over 60 s the person is away from the app, so a 45 s (change) or 300 s (new app) wait mostly delays the run, and assets/prompt/system.md tells the agent not to wait then. A question_id call still waits, so the agent can choose to.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":263},"end":{"line":263},"content_hash":"77a7c4303241981e59ffda79ac3b2acb37b7bb66b87a30debeb041c291ee57f7"},"summary":"Wait on a new question even when no owner surface is open (surface_open false), as the clax-mcp ask does","tags":["revisit:owners answer questions from the notification within a minute of a question asked with no surface open","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/tools/ask_tool.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T23:23:46.066782Z","id":"0c78521c1d305d559ea5aaac6ccf8f4a38852acdcc7584344aef1602fe44e89d","body":{"detail":"AskTool withdraws by itself only on a cancel of the run (RunContext.cancelled). A change that finishes with the question open is parked on purpose: the AskedQuestions entry stays and a late answer runs the change again (R§8). A new app that finishes without the answer, or a change that gives up or stops at a cap with nothing published, leaves the question open in the owner's inbox; for the change its entry would then run a change that already failed and showed Retry. The run's owner (AgentLoop/FeedbackWorker) should call withdrawOpen on those ends, or decide that a Retry also takes the entry.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":356},"end":{"line":373},"content_hash":"95c065abe3c6120c70615f40e0aa6ea64f60d2d7e444d9089900c712273c7b69"},"summary":"For Task A7: call AskTool.withdrawOpen when a new app ends with its question still open, and on a change's give_up or a hard cap without a clean draft","tags":["depends-on-task:A7","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/tools/ask_tool.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T23:23:46.066816Z","id":"6ed6fcd1e85bb6ce10cf54f34f4117fd8dcaf954247b14be3c8f019af3fd4bae","body":{"detail":"The AskedQuestions entry is written as soon as the question is asked, so a late answer can still find the change after an app restart. If the app dies during the wait, the comments were never acknowledged and the worker gets them again on its next feedback poll, so the change runs again while the question stays open with an entry. When the answer arrives later the worker would run the same comments a third time. A7's late-answer path should drop an entry whose comments a later run has answered (the rule R§8 states for a newer viewer comment), or withdraw the question when it reruns those comments without it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":246},"end":{"line":258},"content_hash":"14928f1750fd4f8cbab8f49414c575f0fc70608141f87aac4d49b22ca8c52b80"},"summary":"For Task A7: an entry is put before the wait, so a run killed mid-wait leaves an entry for comments that recovery may run again","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/tools/finish.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T23:27:42.344300Z","id":"3817c74ac49f860fa821818677013d7b3c535f086f9d5ce5e15fd1e891b7f299","body":{"detail":"ChangeLedger records are keyed by artifact ID and base version (apps/clax_app/lib/agent/ledger.dart), and a new app has no ID until the create answers, so finish cannot write one before the call. A Retry from the New sheet after such an ending may make a second app. Recovery can tell: list the artifacts (ClaxApi.listArtifacts) once the daemon answers and look for one whose version 1 was published by the app session (VersionInfo.sessionId, agentHarness 'app') with the run's reply as its note (cleanLine of the note starts with the reply, as madeBy in apps/clax_app/lib/agent/tools/finish.dart checks for a change); found, open it instead of retrying.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":336},"end":{"line":344},"content_hash":"a5e1ae1f41324689c664e32f33aef4ad1224632034807f1383f9d2d10360e252"},"summary":"For A7: a new app whose createArtifact got no answer (status 0) ends RunInterrupted with no ledger record, so whether the app exists is unknown; look for it before offering Retry","tags":["handoff","agent","new-app","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/tools/finish.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T23:27:54.601Z","id":"021e3e2f649cfa55ca0daeb6b8eb756380224c1e1133029d593088d2b12bca5f","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:fb3b05a3","summary":"Fixed: after a landed publish every document-step failure but status 0 goes through _undo (restoreVersion to the base, then _forget); a refused restore forgets the record and the reply says the landed version stays; an app 404 (not_found without a document path) ends RunDropped. Tests in apps/clax_app/test/agent/tools/finish_test.dart: 'a re-read that fails after a landed publish restores the version and drops the ledger record' (the 409 batch then 500 getDoc scenario: restoreVersion n 1 ifVersion 2, v3 holds the base files, empty ledger), 'an error that is not the daemon's after a landed publish restores the version too', 'a restore that is refused drops the ledger record and says the version stays', 'an app deleted after the publish drops the run'. cd apps/clax_app && flutter test test/agent: +515 ~4, All tests passed.","supersedes":"49ce8342aa876818c3e78ed2a455075afd6da3cd1f2899f992c6833b8db5fe96","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/tools/finish.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T23:27:54.601870Z","id":"0398eb4fd723832a9bd6500081793b8bbcf5602f5001e0044f98d4682de9afb1","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:fb3b05a3","summary":"Fixed: RunFinished.docsRefused (apps/clax_app/lib/agent/tools/toolbox.dart) carries why a new app's starting documents were not written, including an unanswered batch, and finish's result names it as docs_refused, for the making screen to say the app was made without its starting data. Tests 'starting documents that are refused are reported with the made app' and 'made with its documents, nothing is reported refused' in apps/clax_app/test/agent/tools/finish_test.dart pass (flutter test test/agent: +515 ~4). The status-0 createArtifact part cannot take a ledger record (no artifact ID before the answer); how recovery finds the app is handed to A7 in record 3817c74a.","supersedes":"2193e695ee47072ca8b4451171f50ae51f8b8e1afdb3825f7371bbe5137ec561","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/tools/finish.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T23:27:54.602574Z","id":"cadb88b3b2222a0d00322d71e39b25e544a13515efaaa9f0eeb0636ae2dd3ade","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"684d15e9c2f996691cc7fa3923d284974e90b6d16a7e858be65eb3567d2e2492","summary":"Since fb3b05a3: a new app's RunFinished.docsRefused is non-null when it was made without its starting documents (the UI should say so), and an app deleted between the publish and the document batch ends RunDropped. A status-0 createArtifact: record 3817c74a.","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/tools/ask_tool.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T23:30:12.334861Z","id":"233067f577a7a075fc226b160caa8fb257a972d2e09cb5b7259826b475c38b4e","body":{"detail":"FeedbackWorker._poll (apps/clax_app/lib/agent/worker.dart) polls feedback while _drain runs a change. When a change's ask wait ends open and the run carries on, an answer given then is handed to that poll as a late answer (docs/contract.md, 'Late answers': the daemon wakes the feedback polls once no ask wait holds the question), and A7's late-answer path takes the AskedQuestions entry and queues a re-run. If the still-running agent then calls ask with the question_id, the daemon hands the same answer over again (contract, '`ask`': 'may see the answer twice'), _settled uses it and _forget drops an entry that is already gone, so the run applies the answer and the queued re-run applies it again to the same comments. Checked against a real daemon (clax at 4176445a): an open question answered with no wait holding it came back in the next pollFeedback's answers.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":317},"end":{"line":322},"content_hash":"34c9f7f78bc60e96c749558ea2879accbec02c465d7b3adf943098a62e5c1ef4"},"suggested_fix":"In A7, defer a late answer whose question is the open question of the run in progress (AskTool.questionId while AskTool.open) until that run ends, then re-run only if the run finished without it (its entry is still there); or have AskTool record answers it handed to the agent so the worker skips them.","summary":"For Task A7: a late answer the worker's feedback poll takes while the asking run is still going can run the change twice","tags":["review","depends-on-task:A7","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/tools/ask_tool.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T23:30:12.335003Z","id":"c53344c12e0f970f5acd59fe4f8b8338f0b81abda101f4d22eee00d215e247bf","body":{"detail":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-12-flutter-app-round2-design.md R§8 'Background' says the agent is told the owner may not be there and should not wait, and assets/prompt/system.md says the same; AskTool enforcing it on the asking call only saves a turn of a wait the prompt forbids. With the app holding the questions topic for its life (plan Task U6), surface_open is false for the app's own run only when its stream has been down past the 60 s grace, a broken surface rather than an away owner, so parking (change) or carrying on (new app) is right. A question_id call still waits. Checked against a real daemon: with no stream the asking call returned status open, call_again true, surface_open false at once, and cancel then withdrew it.","kind":"comment","references":"852bbee73692d54e1b3886dc8283eb27cf7e5e891fc573606dac58f5dccf4976","summary":"Review: not waiting when surface_open is false fits the app; keep it","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/tools/ask_tool.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T23:30:12.335049Z","id":"69f2ce83b2f07603293caf3d12ec05e1734cf4a3de485f7c1a20bc0d1c185517","body":{"detail":"Writing the entry at ask time is what lets a change parked by a kill after the ask still be found, so moving the put to the run's end is not better. The fix is in the worker: before running a change, take every AskedQuestions entry whose commentIds intersect the run's items' comment IDs and withdraw its question (ClaxApi.withdrawQuestion; a 409 question_closed is already swallowed), so the re-run owns those comments and the owner's inbox does not keep a duplicate question. About ten lines in apps/clax_app/lib/agent/worker.dart, testable with MemoryAskedQuestions and FakeClaxApi.","kind":"comment","references":"6ed6fcd1e85bb6ce10cf54f34f4117fd8dcaf954247b14be3c8f019af3fd4bae","summary":"Review: cheap to prevent in A7, and it belongs there","tags":["depends-on-task:A7","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/tools/finish.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T23:56:56.802187Z","id":"bd64a8921ad22cd6131d821d07838e8ec06a356cf9d4f8021f3d450825b8ce50","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:7de1c0e9","summary":"Fixed in 7de1c0e9: AgentLoop._runTools (apps/clax_app/lib/agent/loop.dart) calls FinishTool.attach(toolbox) and wraps capStop to note a tool ended the run, so a cap stop is answered by finish and not answered twice. Tests in apps/clax_app/test/agent/loop_test.dart: 'a cap with no clean draft replies once and publishes nothing', 'a cap after a clean render publishes that draft, saying it stopped early, and leaves the thread open'. flutter test test/agent test/app_background_test.dart test/app_test.dart test/ui/thread_detail_test.dart: +623, all passed.","supersedes":"684d15e9c2f996691cc7fa3923d284974e90b6d16a7e858be65eb3567d2e2492","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/tools/ask_tool.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T23:56:56.802963Z","id":"64ac797727c25224ccb602a6a6adeb2e4a91970fec1a5fd8414991ec17aff73d","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:7de1c0e9","summary":"Fixed in 7de1c0e9: AgentLoop calls AskTool.withdrawOpen after every new app's run, and after a change that ended RunGaveUp (give_up, a cap with no clean draft, a runner-made ending) or RunDropped; a change that finished with its question open is parked. Tests in apps/clax_app/test/agent/loop_test.dart: 'a question still open when the new app ends is withdrawn', group 'change questions' ('…is parked: the question and its entry stay', '…gives up withdraws its open question and forgets it', 'a cap with no clean draft withdraws the open question', 'a runner-made ending withdraws the open question'). flutter test test/agent test/app_background_test.dart test/app_test.dart test/ui/thread_detail_test.dart: +623, all passed.","supersedes":"0c78521c1d305d559ea5aaac6ccf8f4a38852acdcc7584344aef1602fe44e89d","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/tools/ask_tool.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T23:56:56.803706Z","id":"8277e5c00e99b99c19dcf489801275bf5ae96e5ba5913c326fde9436b8faec2d","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:7de1c0e9","summary":"Fixed in 7de1c0e9: AgentLoop.change (apps/clax_app/lib/agent/loop.dart, _takeOverQuestions) first takes every AskedEntry whose commentIds overlap the run's comments and withdraws its question as the run's session, before it marks the app working. Test 'before a change runs, an earlier question asked for its comments is taken and withdrawn' in apps/clax_app/test/agent/loop_test.dart. flutter test test/agent test/app_background_test.dart test/app_test.dart test/ui/thread_detail_test.dart: +623, all passed.","supersedes":"6ed6fcd1e85bb6ce10cf54f34f4117fd8dcaf954247b14be3c8f019af3fd4bae","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/tools/ask_tool.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T23:56:56.804436Z","id":"23e3bd8af48aa878bef80c42b38a5a366606f40e3a25d9b19b1e503812ff81e2","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:7de1c0e9","summary":"Fixed in 7de1c0e9: FeedbackWorker (apps/clax_app/lib/agent/worker.dart) queues a poll's late answer as a job and takes its AskedEntry only when that job runs, after the run in progress; an entry the asking run already dropped (its own ask got the answer) means nothing runs. Test 'late answers an answer the asking run took itself is not run again' in apps/clax_app/test/agent/worker_test.dart (the answer is polled mid-run, the run asks again with the question_id, one run, one version). flutter test test/agent test/app_background_test.dart test/app_test.dart test/ui/thread_detail_test.dart: +623, all passed.","supersedes":"233067f577a7a075fc226b160caa8fb257a972d2e09cb5b7259826b475c38b4e","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/tools/finish.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T23:56:56.808782Z","id":"2b101b148ff8c6d7f3d8c64f61af92dfd4f74d49aa2e8f727502b8eb6e3f9b87","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:7de1c0e9","summary":"Fixed in 7de1c0e9: AgentLoop._newAppTools (apps/clax_app/lib/agent/loop.dart, _findCreated) answers a RunInterrupted create by listing the artifacts and returning one that was not there before the run and whose version 1 the app session published; else it throws, saying to look for the app before trying again. Tests in apps/clax_app/test/agent/loop_test.dart: 'a create whose answer was lost after it landed returns the app it made', 'a create that got no answer and did not land says to look for the app before trying again'. flutter test test/agent test/app_background_test.dart test/app_test.dart test/ui/thread_detail_test.dart: +623, all passed.","supersedes":"3817c74ac49f860fa821818677013d7b3c535f086f9d5ce5e15fd1e891b7f299","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/tools/finish.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T23:56:56.817046Z","id":"ee765454611f2120ef77db6cc6b2aa0f3dcc12aa8b1898dc428d3183e5cd10d0","body":{"detail":"The gate counts a staged db_write as a change (Draft.changedFrom), so a documents-only change must render clean before finish writes the owner's data, as a file change must. Not taken because a render over the draft's document copy is the only check that the page still loads with the new data; it costs one render turn (a change has 2) on a data-only answer.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":201},"end":{"line":225},"content_hash":"4b76645a45ae7b738c25126d9361f5268b39f9e57373b82dc3c6f972e83de41d"},"summary":"Let a finish whose only change is staged document writes skip the render","supersedes":"e260cdd0b2dd761f8aeed2466fc6564cb7ef4d3a72bbb30cc711c4a964f6bdf9","tags":["agent","finish","revisit:data-only changes need their render budget for something else","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/tools/finish.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T23:56:56.817789Z","id":"76578be71b2020f30aaf47e20916c9f725ef76d96b924875ab47de415f94160c","body":{"detail":"Not taken: a re-pinned set or delete replaces or removes what the person wrote since the run read the document, and a re-pinned update overwrites every field its patch names, including an entry the person added to an array field (docs/superpowers/plans/2026-10-12-flutter-app-round2.md Review Focus 1: never overwrite the person's entry). The finish tool's _writeDocs re-reads instead and only drops a write the moved document already holds (a delete of a gone document, a set or update that changes nothing); a moved document that does not hold the write fails the change, after restoring the version before it, and the threads offer Retry. Cost: a change whose update touches fields the person did not change (round 1's 'a document conflict re-reads and writes once more', apps/clax_app/test/agent/loop_test.dart:614) now fails instead of merging. The draft keeps only the version each document was read at (Draft.pins), not its data, so a field-level check of what the person changed is not possible here.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":824},"end":{"line":867},"content_hash":"c54eeaa4a3cd81735198213c4ce5b29fec4edfd700544f86057015de98722d75"},"summary":"On a document conflict at finish, re-pin each write to the version read again and send it once more (the round-1 _writeDocs rule, lib/agent/loop.dart:778-812, and R§4.5 step 3's 'one re-read and retry')","supersedes":"8ac3085d17c79d4cac81103c2fd83ab13091c1ea3b251bcf1cf81db86f85f02b","tags":["agent","finish","data-safety","revisit:changes fail often because the page wrote a document mid-run","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/tools/finish.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T23:56:56.818534Z","id":"9b71118ca578e31672d0425be139ad9c0f4f451aa4108819f2fbbea52569daf6","body":{"detail":"capStop publishes the last clean snapshot of a new app; finish refuses a new app without a title, but a cap cannot ask the model again, so _create falls back to the title the render served the draft under (RenderTool's _untitled, apps/clax_app/lib/agent/tools/render_tool.dart). The owner sees an app named 'New app' and renames it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":316},"end":{"line":326},"content_hash":"fb46b91c49ad7787d053844bdeb285a8aecbc431d79880a31f55dd76bc3e5ecd"},"suggested_fix":"Have A7 pass a title derived from the request (its first words) for a cap stop, or have the prompt (assets/prompt/system.md) ask for set_meta before the first render.","summary":"A new app stopped at a cap before set_meta gave it a title is created as 'New app'","supersedes":"00f142bc0a6d8ea7ac47382642084468b3c1be39743828ee445dd1fc89f353cc","tags":["agent","caps","new-app","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/tools/render_tool.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T02:20:06.897840Z","id":"4f856c5938b50ae0eb1c0a227aca7dcd5305c3a8460c9ed6ebce849fbf821d75","body":{"detail":"createDraft(of: the app) copies the app's live documents at each test run, then the staged writes are applied. The draft's copy (made at the run's first render) can differ: the page's own writes during the page-check load are absent, and documents the person changed since the first render are newer. Tests that depend on what the page wrote on load, or on documents as the first render saw them, can pass or fail differently from the render's page check. The daemon refuses a draft of a draft (crates/clax-core/src/store/drafts.rs create_draft), so copying the draft's documents would need a daemon route.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":244},"end":{"line":312},"content_hash":"884043ac7d3c19e9bfa845ac7eaccf7d17c4fd944d2ffbd0b657fdcebea8d6dc"},"summary":"The test run's scratch draft copies the app's documents as they are at the test run, not the draft's own copy","tags":["agent","render","tests","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/tools/kit_tool.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T02:20:31.258710Z","id":"0fabebcf5c8ac2781a75bd185bfd4b12aa5b15d88b861e7b8521349251c21970","body":{"detail":"Only the icon names are checked against icons.js (test/agent/tools/kit_tool_test.dart, 'every kit file is a bundled asset'). A prop or export renamed in apps/clax_app/assets/kit/kit.js or chart.js leaves the model told the old name, with no failing test. A test that imports the export names of each module and checks each named in _api would catch it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":102},"end":{"line":168},"content_hash":"8ab4b2363110a0c06b24268a162449430ab2888ad94558c9ac6ba47ed33773ac"},"summary":"The API text add_kit returns restates kit.js, chart.js and icons.js by hand and can drift from them","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/tools/render_tool.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T02:23:43.842509Z","id":"4b908f1e3a799480aaedc5b2e13e42d14845be7e23b050544f43d71546f2df16","body":{"detail":"Failure: a new app whose first render loads index.html without uncaught errors, with tests/*.test.js, started when less than testLimit + _testSlack (40 s) of the wall clock is left. s.budget.whenTimeUp (line 272) ends the run with noRun('The run is out of time …'), a TestRun with one failed entry; render then calls markRendered(snap, testsFailed: true) (line 223), Draft.markRendered leaves lastClean null (apps/clax_app/lib/agent/tools/draft.dart:212-215), and FinishTool.capStop (apps/clax_app/lib/agent/tools/finish.dart:260-267) replies 'Couldn't make that change: it ran out of time' though the page rendered clean and no test failed. The same holds for an infrastructure noRun (createDraft ClaxApiError, the harness not answering): only tests that ran and failed are failing tests (spec 2026-10-12-flutter-real-apps-design C2).","kind":"blocker","span":{"start":{"line":269},"end":{"line":285},"content_hash":"65280b515b9212ef916c5e9d4192d90caafb59374c8382fd1a381727790a67c7"},"suggested_fix":"Distinguish a run that did not complete (time up, cancel, could not serve) from failed tests: keep the snapshot as lastClean (or a separate lastErrorFree) when the tests did not finish, while finish still refuses it; test with a fake clock firing whenTimeUp during FakeInspector.runTests, then capStop publishes the snapshot.","summary":"A test run cut by the run's wall clock counts as failing tests, so a clean first render near the cap never becomes lastClean and the cap stop publishes nothing","tags":["review","review:T1","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/tools/finish.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T02:23:43.842625Z","id":"0cd9d0685277bea06e793be7987350b97ddc349775b424247b2c813788c5e828","body":{"detail":"capStop publishes only Draft.cleanOnBase, which since 05f1e455 requires passing tests. A model that writes one wrong test in a new app and runs out of turns or time leaves the person with no app and 'Couldn't make that change'. This matches the C2 text ('publishes the last render with passing tests') but the alternative, publishing the last error-free render when none passed its tests (with the stopped-early reply saying tests failed), keeps the work. Owner's call.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":260},"end":{"line":267},"content_hash":"aa9a4cbfe1acb2a4111aff3df56a27e0674b6ecb3eb0f41d0426b6465b38d206"},"summary":"A new app whose only clean renders have failing tests gets nothing at a cap stop, even though its page loads without errors","tags":["review","review:T1","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/tools/render_tool.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T02:23:43.842680Z","id":"c0a3e8f641e5a69c3c2b03fb880ad5b357aa62b6c78abc31fc893fff3ca026d3","body":{"detail":"_runTests runs after Inspector.inspect returns: api.createDraft (copying up to the draft document limit of the app's documents), _writeOps of every staged write, a fresh WebView load, the tests (up to 30 s), then a delete. None of it overlaps the inspection. Creating the scratch draft and writing its documents while the inspection settles would hide the daemon round trips; the second page load is inherent to C2.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":244},"end":{"line":268},"content_hash":"fe3901ca4167ff46d4f73a1ac8f254a9d700ea70b940eeb0607e31252cc155ca"},"suggested_fix":"Start createDraft + _writeOps concurrently with the inspection (discard the scratch draft when the page has uncaught errors), and measure render latency with and without tests in the perf gate.","summary":"Each render of a draft with tests pays a second draft creation, document copy, staged-write batch and full page load after the inspection, serially","tags":["review","review:T1","perf","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/tools/kit_tool.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T02:23:53.471280Z","id":"875ca94e26fc37a996b70ce7b041798df20bc98ede796fe70b64d10733642bb1","body":{"detail":"_api is hand-written; today it matches (all kit.js exports present except getDb, Toast, TabBar, intentionally internal; preact.js exports useLayoutEffect as listed; kit.css classes exist). A test that reads assets/kit/kit.js and chart.js, collects export names by regex and asserts each is named in _api (or on an internal allow-list) catches drift cheaply; generating the text from JSDoc is more work than it saves. Related record: 0fabebcf5c8ac2781a75bd185bfd4b12aa5b15d88b861e7b8521349251c21970.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":101},"end":{"line":168},"content_hash":"712e7de15424b749e438cdd167b61357c8152d456da5b91069967ce63107c726"},"summary":"Check the add_kit API text against the kit's exports in a test","tags":["review","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/tools/render_tool.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T02:27:16.973006Z","id":"1aa0738990055adaa41f3f3dfb113f44f13e927ca1480484cb5cd3b24e43fa95","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:0429cde7","summary":"Fixed: RenderTool._runTests returns a String reason for a run the wall clock, a cancel, the daemon or a silent harness cut short; render reports it as tests: {not_run: why} and marks the render without testsFailed, so it stays lastClean. Tests in apps/clax_app/test/agent/tools/render_tool_test.dart: 'a test run cut by the wall clock is not run and leaves the render clean' and 'a test run that did not happen is not run, says why, and is no test failure'. cd apps/clax_app && flutter test test/agent/tools/render_tool_test.dart test/agent/tools/finish_test.dart: +91, All tests passed.","supersedes":"4b908f1e3a799480aaedc5b2e13e42d14845be7e23b050544f43d71546f2df16","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/tools/render_tool.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T02:27:16.974067Z","id":"705fc718b794faf170256d724141cf8723403691dda2f38e3c66a2e0cc5588d5","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:0429cde7","summary":"Fixed: render starts RenderTool._makeScratch (createDraft and the staged writes) before Inspector.inspect and awaits it only for the test run; a page check that fails deletes the unused scratch draft. Test 'a page with uncaught errors runs no tests, and the scratch draft made meanwhile is deleted' in apps/clax_app/test/agent/tools/render_tool_test.dart passes (+91 with finish_test.dart). The second page load stays, as C2 requires.","supersedes":"c0a3e8f641e5a69c3c2b03fb880ad5b357aa62b6c78abc31fc893fff3ca026d3","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/tools/finish.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T02:27:16.974978Z","id":"cb8d32ce74445dd1f12635f86dfa18e7340635d0171c3da30c14e42b9a843fb8","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"0cd9d0685277bea06e793be7987350b97ddc349775b424247b2c813788c5e828","summary":"Decided (by the coordinating agent of the round-3 build, issuer_type ai, not the owner; the owner may overrule): at a cap stop with no render whose tests passed, FinishTool.capStop publishes the last render without uncaught errors (Draft.pageCleanOnBase) and the stopped-early reply adds 'Some of its checks failed.'; finish outside the cap still refuses failing tests. Reason: the owner's rule \"Always render first\" (spec 2026-10-12-flutter-app-round2-design RA2, record 47fc0696) is kept, since that snapshot rendered; a failing test should not cost the person the whole app. Implemented in 0429cde7; test 'at the time cap with no render whose tests passed, publishes the last render without uncaught errors and says checks failed' in apps/clax_app/test/agent/tools/finish_test.dart.","tags":["status:decided","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/tools/kit_tool.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T02:27:36.631577Z","id":"20e37544e5c2c5732bc10e1d852487b2f4ab89aa1fe2eaedf06492af22a340a2","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:c6adf244","summary":"kit_tool_test 'every kit file is a bundled asset' now checks every export of kit.js and chart.js is named in the API text; getDb, Toast and TabBar were added. flutter test test/agent/tools/kit_tool_test.dart: +5 all passed.","supersedes":"875ca94e26fc37a996b70ce7b041798df20bc98ede796fe70b64d10733642bb1","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/tools/kit_tool.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T21:09:58.384656Z","id":"b8156e4790b3c0398d45fb00bb269b8441f9f7e283279d59f7e36de2d60bc8c4","body":{"detail":"In the agent's renders and tests net calls fail not_granted (apps/clax_app/assets/prompt/system.md lines 230-233; concern 8454afd7 and its reply c86eceaa), so a correct map renders 'Map tiles need permission ... not allowed to reach tile.openstreetmap.org'. system.md says net is off in renders in general, but next to a screenshot that reads like an error the model may 'fix' the map: drop it, change hosts, or draw its own. One sentence where the map is described costs little.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":157},"end":{"line":172},"content_hash":"d4c175fa633cbc939d2a26439292d1953ddd584630183d499549e1b3fc670584"},"suggested_fix":"Append to the 'map.js' entry: 'In your renders net is off, so the map shows its \"Map tiles need permission\" note instead of tiles: that is expected; keep the map and its net declaration.'","summary":"kitApi's map entry does not tell the agent that its own renders show the permission note instead of tiles","tags":["review","agent-guidance","K3","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/tools/kit_tool.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T01:43:18.709489Z","id":"00d182d55c8e40ddf4e15517766ac0febb3809c8cb11072603f9b2ef1851560e","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:a17ecb7b","summary":"Fixed in a17ecb7b: the map entry says the agent's renders show real tiles once the tile host is granted and a grey \"Map preview\" grid before, both expected. flutter test test/agent/tools passes; scripts/sync-app-prompt.sh --check exit 0 for this change.","supersedes":"b8156e4790b3c0398d45fb00bb269b8441f9f7e283279d59f7e36de2d60bc8c4","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/tools/finish.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T15:36:18.989544Z","id":"d2e75672ac9dfd73004befaf951f0846d5b0fc2f117d185071eab5f62bcdb654","body":{"detail":"GiveUpTool treats any give_up of a change made once RunBudget.nearLimit is non-null (soft note active: two turns left or 60% of time, tokens or cost, or no render left) as a limit stop: the reply says the change was too big for one go and offers Keep going, with the agent's reason under 'The agent said:'. A give_up late in a run for a reason Keep going cannot fix (it needs a camera) gets that wording and a Keep going that will fail the same way.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":755},"end":{"line":775},"content_hash":"f16326029cf15ea8e1add596263a833674a3271981501a0c7e7f42f2d6cc9ead"},"suggested_fix":"Give give_up an optional boolean (out_of_room) the prompt asks for, within the tool-schema limits, and name the limit only when it is set or a hard cap is reached.","summary":"A give_up near a cap for a reason other than room is worded as the limit","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/tools/finish.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T15:40:29.348811Z","id":"8168af95979e40eed81f14c67bd0131bdfff62568c89b1a66ec0804a8ed47459","body":{"detail":"Failure: a change run that calls give_up({reason: 'this needs the camera, which apps here cannot use'}) after 72 seconds of its 120 (60% of RunCaps.change wallClock), after its 8th turn, or after its 3rd render. RunBudget.nearLimit (lib/agent/tools/budget.dart:263-279) is non-null in every one of those states, which is most of a change run that has tried anything, so GiveUpTool (lines 755-770) replies \"Couldn't make that change: it was too big for one go — it needed more than 2 minutes. Tap Keep going to pick up where it stopped.\" with the real reason only under 'The agent said:'. Keep going runs again, gives up again near a cap, and offers Keep going again, until the change's $6 is spent. The prompt makes this the common case: apps/clax_app/assets/prompt/system.md:56-57 says give_up 'only when the request cannot be done in a web page here', while lines 48-55 tell the agent to put what is done and left 'in that reason' when out of time, so give_up means either thing and the code cannot tell which. The test 'a give_up far from every cap' (test/agent/loop_limits_test.dart:126) gives up on turn 1, the only state where the wording is right.","kind":"blocker","span":{"start":{"line":749},"end":{"line":771},"content_hash":"46cf38e246969303856935bcbc7c3932162debdfd2aa995b8993a92c7f29b519"},"suggested_fix":"Give give_up an optional out_of_room boolean, ask for it in system.md's give_up and Mind the caps bullets (true only when the work fits a web page and more steps would finish it), and name the limit only when it is true or a hard cap was reached; otherwise reply failureReply(reason) and keep nothing. Add a test: give_up with out_of_room false after 8 turns replies the plain failure.","summary":"A change's give_up for a reason Keep going cannot fix is told as 'too big for one go' and offers Keep going","supersedes":"d2e75672ac9dfd73004befaf951f0846d5b0fc2f117d185071eab5f62bcdb654","tags":["review","X5","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/tools/finish.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T15:57:46.194800Z","id":"133e23e8e89df6a3bb657222fb9f65c8d9bf074ca8001b94a1e4124869698b0c","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:e4cefaf3","summary":"Fixed in e4cefaf3/e41fba35: give_up takes an optional out_of_room boolean; only out_of_room give_ups (named by RunBudget.mostSpent) and real cap stops get the limit wording and Keep going; any other give_up replies failureReply(reason) and keeps nothing. system.md's give_up bullet now names both cases. Test 'a give_up near a cap without out_of_room replies the plain failure and keeps nothing' in test/agent/loop_limits_test.dart; strict_limits_test passes. flutter test (apps/clax_app, whole suite): +1702 ~122, all passed; flutter analyze: no issues; scripts/sync-app-prompt.sh --check: OK.","supersedes":"8168af95979e40eed81f14c67bd0131bdfff62568c89b1a66ec0804a8ed47459","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/tools/kit_tool.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T14:54:52.512116Z","id":"c0015ac01c53cbbf46b62b9e65828e4041ad52b968a88f812681ebaacb703502","body":{"detail":"An agent run on the home app keeps the file from the bundle; an agent asked to add the kit afresh, or a home app built from scratch, has no way to get it. Adding a 'home' part (fake-home.js) and documenting it in the prompt is the agent-kit step of the home-screen plan (docs/superpowers/plans/2026-10-16-home-screen-app.md Task 6).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":18},"end":{"line":23},"content_hash":"d4941c8ed796769677b4a6baed3ddaae8515b27d3f002e9b4df85fb7f13a91ac"},"summary":"add_kit has no part for fake-home.js, so only the shipped home app (which carries kit/fake-home.js in its bundle, apps/clax_app/home/manifest.json kit) can test against the fake home capability","tags":["home-app","kit","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/tools/kit_tool.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T15:35:57.478216Z","id":"934eede2f93b5a130aec36b3a2b1dd52b289627939dacb38b9bed02c521e2a4b","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:32e01cd4","summary":"kitParts has a 'home' part bringing fake-home.js, and kitApi describes fakeHome for the agent (tool result and system prompt). Test kit_tool_test.dart 'home brings the fake home capability, for a home app's tests': flutter test test/agent/tools/kit_tool_test.dart test/agent/prompt_test.dart, all passed.","supersedes":"c0015ac01c53cbbf46b62b9e65828e4041ad52b968a88f812681ebaacb703502","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/tools/finish.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T03:35:42.703267Z","id":"99051011150fd0cbc7ae28535e2277710e5e51a56f1f46c39c684bfad3398c38","body":{"detail":"capStop's limitFailureReply(cap, leftUsd: left) gets no agentSaid: the run's narration is left out on purpose, so each stop of a change whose draft never rendered clean posts 'Couldn't make that change: it was too big for one go — it needed more than 10 steps. Tap Keep going to pick up where it stopped.' (the $-left sentence is added only under $3). No version lands and the kept edits (UnfinishedChange.edits) are not shown anywhere, so the thread page (lib/ui/thread_detail.dart _statusCard) and the Working chip read the same after each press; the narration is visible only while a run goes, in the change sheet. Options: (a) quote the run's last narration or the kept notes in the reply as 'The agent said'; (b) list what the kept draft changed (paths, or the plan items marked) in the reply or the status card; (c) count the presses ('stopped 3 times, $2.10 of $6 spent') in the reply. Recommended: (a) with (c), a small change in failure.dart and capStop; (b) needs UI design.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":276},"end":{"line":290},"content_hash":"0adb1cb224d56e5f47632606f0ee20d077582bd75bb461fa2fa9a56539081a94"},"summary":"A cap stop with nothing to publish replies the same words every time, so repeated Keep goings show no progress","tags":["keep-going","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/tools/budget.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T03:35:42.703380Z","id":"c8bd94b3856eceef01269da8558e8e07a2ceffcff8c6000b40113e53a7f1a597","body":{"detail":"Each Keep going is another RunCaps.change run (10 turns, 3 renders, 120 s, at most $1.50; softNote tells it to finish once 2 turns are left or 72 s are spent). A Keep going run first spends turns on what the earlier run already did: 'Render first' (lib/agent/prompt.dart _writeKeepGoing) costs a turn and one of the 3 renders, and files past PromptBuilder.maxInlineBytes (24 KB) are not in the first message, so they are read again. What remains for new work is about 4 to 6 turns a press. Nothing bounds the presses but changeCapUsd ($6, lib/agent/failure.dart), which stops a sixth press only when each run costs about $1 or more; the first message still says 'First decide whether this change fits one run', with nothing telling the agent this change already stopped N times. Options: (a) after the second stop, have the Keep going run plan_set the rest as plan features and let continue runs (RunCaps.continueBuild: 18 turns, 240 s, chained by the worker) build it; (b) run a Keep going at RunCaps.continueBuild's caps; (c) continue automatically within the $6 without a press; (d) raise RunCaps.change.turns. Recommended: (a), with the stop count in the Keep going message, since it uses the build path built for big work and shows progress as the plan's checklist; (b) as the smaller step.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":39},"end":{"line":45},"content_hash":"1ee9445eaaff7da650d8d3b77dbb85338f05936abda94a9ea5df6336589e2dc2"},"summary":"Keep going reruns a 10-turn change run each press and never turns a change that keeps stopping into a build","tags":["keep-going","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/tools/budget.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T04:13:12.143912Z","id":"dc00ea9717534bd2a926eaf215f7d004c10482db4e77d193085235cc674249b2","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"c8bd94b3856eceef01269da8558e8e07a2ceffcff8c6000b40113e53a7f1a597","summary":"Owner's decision (relayed by the coordinating agent, 2026-10-16): option (a). After a change's second limit stop its Keep going run puts the rest of the work into plan features and the build's continue runs (18 turns, chained by the worker) finish it; progress shows as the plan's checklist. Every run is told how many times the change has stopped.","tags":["status:decided","decision","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/tools/finish.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T04:13:12.144061Z","id":"721d5114adaf3d59b0db1cf1e7e02f7ec1de89074ca9acd1a89f3950006323d3","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"99051011150fd0cbc7ae28535e2277710e5e51a56f1f46c39c684bfad3398c38","summary":"Owner's decision (relayed by the coordinating agent, 2026-10-16): all three options. A limit stop's reply quotes the agent's latest kept notes, says the count and spend ('Stopped 3 times · $2.10 of $6 used'), and names in its text, with no new widget, the files the kept draft changed with added and removed line counts ('Changed so far: index.html (+42 −10), app.js (+8)'), about five files then 'and N more'.","tags":["status:decided","decision","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/tools/budget.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T04:13:12.144181Z","id":"dc2549622e6b37931b2acac60f214a63affb3b938d5f99dc57b1d099a80d90d1","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:e35c7af8","summary":"Done as decided: UnfinishedChange.stops counts the limit stops; each Keep going run's first message says how often the change stopped (PromptBuilder._writeKeepGoing); from planAfterStops (2, lib/agent/failure.dart) the run is told to plan_set what is left as todo features and finish the draft, and FeedbackWorker._runOne starts the build after a Keep going even when it failed again. Evidence: flutter test test/agent/worker_limits_test.dart passes 'each run is told how often the change stopped, and after the second stop Keep going plans the rest, which the build then builds even when that run stops too'; with the worker's ChangeFailed clause removed it fails.","supersedes":"c8bd94b3856eceef01269da8558e8e07a2ceffcff8c6000b40113e53a7f1a597","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/tools/finish.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T04:13:12.154043Z","id":"496d26729f32dd70d430c1434f5f46402153d66317c0b2366b0692a9a3e3f973","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:083f43c7","summary":"Done as decided: limitFailureReply and limitLandedReply take a LimitProgress (lib/agent/failure.dart, limitProgressText) built by limitProgress in lib/agent/tools/finish.dart from the run context's earlier stops and notes, the run's narrations and the draft's kept edits (line counts from lib/agent/line_diff.dart). Evidence: flutter test test/agent passes 'a second stop says how often the change stopped, what its runs cost, the files its draft changed and the latest notes of both runs' (test/agent/loop_limits_test.dart, failed against the previous lib) and the limitProgressText group in test/agent/line_diff_test.dart; CLAX_KG_SHOTS=1 flutter test --update-goldens test/ui/keep_going_shots_test.dart renders the thread page with the reply and Keep going, light and dark.","supersedes":"99051011150fd0cbc7ae28535e2277710e5e51a56f1f46c39c684bfad3398c38","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
